       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**The problem:** Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. Usual dosing is:\n- **Start:** 25\u201350 mg once daily\n- **Usual range:** 50\u2013200 mg/day\n- **Max:** 200 mg/day\n\nAt 1000 mg/day, the risks include serotonin syndrome, QTc prolongation, seizures and other toxicity. It could be a typo for **100 mg**, which is a common dose.\n\n**Can you confirm which you meant?**\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg** by mouth once daily\n2. **Another dose** (please specify)\n3. **1000 mg as written.** If so, please tell me the reason so I can add it to the order note for pharmacy review.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
